   {
     "heading": "5. Public, social, and historical competitive data",
-    "body": "Some data is visible to other users when you use current public or social features. This may include nickname, coin-rank avatar, profile card settings and style, the short profile-card caption you write yourself (available with a Pro profile card), streak, rank, Spire floor, steps and weekly result, weekly coins earned (shown to members of your Spire room), historical Arena and tournament results from earlier app versions, premium markers, friend activity, activity likes, community pack author information, seller notifications, and similar profile fields. Your profile-card caption is visible to other players who open your profile card; other players can report it, and we may remove captions that break our rules. If you answer the daily poll, we store your chosen option linked to your account ID to prevent repeat voting; other users only see aggregated percentages. When you save a video to your favorites, the App may show other users how many people saved that video; this is an aggregated count only and does not reveal who saved it. Visibility depends on the feature: some fields may be public to app users, some visible to friends, some visible to community pack buyers or sellers, and some visible only to moderators/admins.\n\nThe Spire groups players into weekly rooms of up to 30 places for each study language. Other app users who open the room can see your nickname, avatar and cosmetic style, your steps, place and weekly result. Some places in a room may be filled by computer-controlled participants rather than real people. Weekly room records are kept as part of the Spire history; your entry is removed from them when your account is deleted.\n\nWhen you use the Together feature with friends, those friends may see whether you studied today, how many days you both studied on the same day, the resulting friendship level and progress, Friends may also send or receive nudge signals through this feature.\n\nHistorical records created by retired features (such as the old Quiz mode, Arena matches and friend duels, tournaments, clubs, or friend gifts), including old results or participation records, may be retained only as reasonably necessary for security, fraud or abuse prevention, dispute handling, legal compliance, backup expiry, or deletion integrity. Account deletion is designed to delete or de-identify those historical records controlled by Knowly, subject only to the limited retention grounds described in this Policy. Those historical records are not presented as currently available gameplay features."
+    "body": "Some data is visible to other users when you use current public or social features. This may include nickname, coin-rank avatar, profile card settings and style, the short profile-card caption you write yourself (available with a Pro profile card), streak, rank, Spire floor, steps and weekly result, weekly coins earned (shown to members of your Spire room), historical Arena and tournament results from earlier app versions, premium markers, friend activity, activity likes, community pack author information, seller notifications, and similar profile fields. Your profile-card caption is visible to other players who open your profile card; other players can report it, and we may remove captions that break our rules. If you answer the daily poll, we store your chosen option linked to your account ID to prevent repeat voting; other users only see aggregated percentages. When you save a video to your favorites, the App may show other users how many people saved that video; this is an aggregated count only and does not reveal who saved it. Visibility depends on the feature: some fields may be public to app users, some visible to friends, some visible to community pack buyers or sellers, and some visible only to moderators/admins.\n\nThe Spire groups players into weekly rooms of up to 30 places for each study language. Other app users who open the room can see your nickname, avatar and cosmetic style, your steps, place and weekly result. Some places in a room may be filled by computer-controlled participants rather than real people. Weekly room records are kept as part of the Spire history; your entry is removed from them when your account is deleted.\n\nWhen you use the Together feature with friends, those friends may see whether you studied today, how many days you both studied on the same day, the resulting friendship level and progress, Friends may also send or receive nudge signals through this feature.\n\nHistorical records created by retired features (such as the old Quiz mode, Arena matches and friend duels, tournaments, clubs, friend gifts, or the old ideas board (submitted ideas, likes and reports on ideas)), including old results or participation records, may be retained only as reasonably necessary for security, fraud or abuse prevention, dispute handling, legal compliance, backup expiry, or deletion integrity. Account deletion is designed to delete or de-identify those historical records controlled by Knowly, subject only to the limited retention grounds described in this Policy. Those historical records are not presented as currently available gameplay features."
